    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d745">

                <pb facs="0886" n="792" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg792"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.7131/103: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Rumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-07-05T16:00:00+01:44">July 5, 1930—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 5—3 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>24. Department’s telegram 14, July 3, 8 p.m., paragraph (2). Forwarding by the
                    pouch July 7th proposed draft of provisional commercial agreement<anchor n="11"
                        xml:id="d745-f1"/> similar to that which is being submitted to other
                    countries who have not yet concluded commercial treaties. Five articles provide
                    for general reciprocal most-favored-nation treatment in matters of
                    establishment, commerce, industry, customs, tariff rates, taxes, navigation.
                    Agreement to become effective September 1st and to continue in force until March
                    1st, 1931. It is in treaty form but clause requiring ratification has been
                    omitted. Am <pb facs="0887" n="793" xml:id="pg793"/> doubtful however whether in
                    present form it would be valid without Senate approval. Endeavored to secure
                    consent to arrange matter by the exchange of notes but Government considers this
                    method precluded by terms to [<hi rendition="#italic">of</hi>] Rumanian tariff
                    law.</p>
                <p>Was planning to go on leave July 15th for much needed cure. In view of present
                    circumstances does Department wish me to abandon plan?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
